17. NORMAL ATTENDANCE RULE
==================================================

Official class start time:

Example:
10:00 AM

Default late threshold:

20 minutes

Therefore:

Before 10:20 AM:
PRESENT

At or after 10:20 AM:
LATE

The 20-minute threshold MUST NOT be hard-coded in multiple places.

Store it in configurable system/course settings.

==================================================
18. ABSENT RULE
==================================================

A student is considered absent when the attendance session/class is finalized and the student has no valid attendance record.

Valid attendance can come from:

- Successful QR verification
OR
- Successful face verification

depending on the attendance method configured for that session.

Do not mark a student absent merely because a QR or face verification attempt failed temporarily.

==================================================
19. THREE-LATE PENALTY
==================================================

If a student receives three consecutive LATE attendance records for the same course:

3 LATE = 1 ATTENDANCE PENALTY

Do NOT delete or alter the original attendance records.

Maintain separately:

- Actual attendance status
- Late count
- Consecutive late count
- Penalty count
- Effective attendance

Example:

Late
Late
Late

→ One penalty

The original three Late records remain in the database for auditability.

Penalty calculation must be centralized in one business-logic service.

==================================================
20. ATTENDANCE PERCENTAGE
==================================================

Use one centralized attendance calculation engine.

Formula:

Attendance Percentage =
Effective Present Classes / Total Conducted Classes × 100

The calculation must consistently handle:

- Present
- Late
- Absent
- Penalty

No page or route should implement its own attendance percentage formula.

==================================================
21. EXAM ELIGIBILITY
==================================================

Required attendance:

60%

Rule:

Attendance >= 60%
→ Exam Eligible

Attendance < 60%
→ Exam Not Eligible / At Risk

Exactly 60% MUST be considered eligible.

The 60% rule must exist in one centralized service.

==================================================
22. PLANNED AND CONDUCTED CLASSES
==================================================

Each Course Offering must have:

- Planned classes
- Conducted classes
- Remaining classes

Do NOT confuse planned classes with conducted classes.

Example:

Planned:
35

Conducted:
24

Remaining:
11

==================================================
23. MAXIMUM POSSIBLE ATTENDANCE
==================================================

The system must calculate whether the student can still reach 60%.

Example:

Planned classes = 35
Conducted = 24
Effective Present = 13
Remaining = 11

If the student attends every remaining class:

Maximum possible present:
13 + 11 = 24

Maximum possible attendance:
24 / 35 × 100 = 68.57%

The system must calculate:

- Current attendance
- Remaining classes
- Required future attendance
- Maximum possible attendance
- Recoverability

If even perfect attendance in all remaining classes cannot reach 60%, mark the student as:

CRITICAL / NOT RECOVERABLE

==================================================
